{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
  "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Once again, the government is trying to use the open-ended federal fraud statutes to enforce honest government at the state and local levels. Its theory this time is that the defendants committed property fraud by reallocating two traffic lanes from one public road to another without disclosing their real political reason for doing so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You've said that if the resources were diverted to private use, then the prosecution would be okay. But why isn't it a private use to benefit defendants politically?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Roth, on -- on that theory, would it or would it not make a difference if the defendants here, rather than doing everything that they did for a political reason, if they had done it to make their commutes easier or their families' commutes easier, so it wasn't anything about politics, it was their own personal interests, but they did exactly the same things, is that covered or is not -- is that not covered on your theory?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What we're doing here is interpreting a statute. And it's not quite clear to me how your argument fits into the language of this statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEVY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: A public official who is acting politically and not for personal gain does not commit fraud by lying about his reason for an official decision if the decision was generally within his authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The -- the arrangement is always that the -- there's a New York representative who's the executive director and the New Jersey representative who's the deputy; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I think one of the government's main arguments for -- on the sufficiency of the evidence, which is fairly pro-government, and in this situation, was that Mr. Wildstein had to lie to the Port Authority employees about the executive director knowing about this lane change."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The defendants in this case committed fraud by telling a lie to take control over the physical access lanes to the George Washington Bridge and the employee resources necessary to realign them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me start with the legal argument that was made by Kelly's counsel, which seems to be drawing a distinction between public uses and private uses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is about a very specific kind of fraud, commandeering fraud. It is when the defendant tries to take over property that is in the hands of the victim and manage it as if it is his own property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If he had the authority --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What does that say about authorize -- about authority to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Baroni actually had the authority to reallocate the lanes for any reason or no reason, as his counsel just stated to this Court that he did, I don't see how the jury could have found that the lies that they told were material."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, Baroni clearly had significant authority within the Port Authority organization"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ROTH",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "schemes to obtain property. And the government's theory of property here, as I think we just heard, is that the officials, by making this decision about lane alignment, commandeered the control over the George Washington Bridge. That is exactly the type of regulatory control that Cleveland said is not property. Cleveland referred to the intangible rights of allocation, exclusion, and control. And the sovereign's intangible rights of allocation, exclusion, and control are not property for purposes of this statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Why do you call it incidental? I mean, it was essential to the scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d50d6981804f539b69dece1d4726e68c9ee1697ebcc182a3a397edc06a22bd6a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d50d6981804f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if it cost a million dollars? Would it be incidental?"
    },
    {
